    "result_text": "The full test suite passes: **34 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the GOLD membership tier rule. The tier is a computed property on the `Owner` model, so I gave it the household-size data it needs and applied the rule with the correct precedence.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a persisted `householdSize` field (`@Column(name = \"household_size\")`) with getter/setter, and updated `getMembershipTier()` to return `'GOLD'` first when `householdSize >= 3`, otherwise falling through to the existing SILVER/BRONZE logic. Updated the Javadoc accordingly.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 In the create flow, when the owner joins a shared household, it now records `householdSize = householdMembers.size() + 1` (existing members plus the new owner). So the third owner in a shared household gets a size of 3 \u2192 GOLD.\n\n3. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 Added the `household_size INTEGER` column so the field round-trips through persistence (the test creates then re-reads via `GET /api/owners/{id}`).\n\nThe GOLD check takes priority over BRONZE/SILVER; owners not in a 3+ household have `householdSize` null and fall back to the prior rules unchanged, which is confirmed by the passing Cp15 (SILVER/BRONZE) tests.",
